      "natural_statement": "For every fixed smooth source-admissible cutoff chi, the staged cometric in both inward frames satisfies P positive definite, P double-prime negative semidefinite, norm(P), norm(P-prime)/delta <= C0, and |P-prime p|^2 <= C0 delta p^T(-P-double-prime)p for all 0<delta<=min(1/2,m/(2K2)); m,K2,C0 are explicitly defined in REPORT.md Section 1.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [
        {
          "assumption_id": "SRC358_FAMILY",
          "statement": "The manuscript defines a(u)=exp(-1/(2/3-u)) below 2/3 and zero above, A integral a, d1=1+delta A(t), d2=1+delta A(1-t), s=delta^2 chi(t), P=B_s diag(d1,d2) B_s^T; chi is fixed, smooth and nondecreasing with cutoffs 5/12 and 7/12; end frames T1=I and T2=[[delta^2,1],[1,0]]. These are input definitions, not an assumption of cometric-bounds.",
